<div class="hd"><span class="ey">Specialist Notes</span><h2>HCM Specialist Model-Matching Notes</h2></div>
<p style="margin-bottom:18px">After working with buyers exploring JP Medics massage chairs — from first-time premium shoppers to experienced upgraders — the HCM product team has observed clear patterns in how buyers compare Kozue and Kaze Duo.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:18px"><strong style="color:var(--ink)">Common buyer pattern:</strong> JP Medics tends to earn strong satisfaction with buyers who match the right model to their daily routine. The brand's defining strength is delivering a structured, precise massage feel — a controlled experience rather than brute-force intensity.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:18px"><strong style="color:var(--ink)">Strongest features buyers test for:</strong> <span class="mk">structured massage feel</span>, <span class="mk">premium build quality</span>, and <span class="mk">daily-use comfort routine</span>.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:18px"><strong style="color:var(--ink)">Most common expectation gaps:</strong> Buyers accustomed to force-oriented brands may initially find JP Medics more measured. Foot roller intensity for sensitive users and premium pricing are the next most common concerns.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:18px"><strong style="color:var(--ink)">Pre-purchase recommendations:</strong></p>
